                        "review": "this is an interesting game but there are a couple issues I've found on replays.\r\n\r\nBeware unlimited terms like the UK Prime Minister. The game devs didn't put in a retire option and so far I haven't died in office. Several elections there was not a single vote cast for the opposition nor were there any non-voters. Education and Health maxed out, Poverty eliminated, Full Employment, a large Sovereign Fund cushion and over time there are no new laws to introduce unless you just want to swing the country in a different direction. I've had to resort to going through each law on the books and seeing which ones could be eliminated that wouldn't change things much (no reason for a car tax, car usage is nil and so the tax isn't bringing money in, same for tobacco tax) Seriously, winning this hard makes it boring and I don't know how to end the game. I just want to return to my farm and raise goats or something in peace and let a new generation take over and mess up the world I brought them up in.",
